📖 Project Overview
This project demonstrates the integration of CAD, GIS, and Web Mapping tools to process, adjust, and publish spatial data for a real estate plots management system.
The primary goal was to transform CAD-based layouts into GIS formats and visualize the information in an interactive web map using 
Google My Maps for enhanced accessibility and decision-making.

The project provides two viewing modes for end-users:
Project Owner Mode: Detailed insights about each land parcel, including dimensions, ownership, and status.
Common People Mode: General access to explore available plots for potential buyers.


🚀 Project Features

DWG File Management in AutoCAD Map 3D
  Processed and imported CAD layouts in DWG format.
  Designed precise layouts of land parcels.
Spatial Adjustment in ArcGIS
  Performed georeferencing, spatial adjustment, and annotation for accurate mapping.
DXF to GIS Conversion in QGIS
  Converted DXF files to shapefiles and KML formats for web integration.
Interactive Web Maps Using Google My Maps
  Published interactive maps with two user access modes:
      Project Owner Mode: For stakeholders to access parcel-specific details.
      Common People Mode: Simplified map for general users.
Custom Styling and Visualization
  Styled maps in QGIS with color-coded plots and exported as KML for enhanced user experience.


